'''
    解題黑вия Digit2String
    * Leetcode define 1 <= s.length <= 1000 It means 0 <= s.length <= 1000 which means input may be empty string.
    * Leetcode define s consists of digits and the '#' letter. It means input not only exist digits, but also ',./;()\=_+-|][{}:<>?'.
    * Comment on above code
        1. const char INTAB[123] means INTAB size is 123.
            but why size is 123 instead of 200?
            Because 0-9 is not part of input.
            refer 0-9
                \0 → \108 → ... time 3 → \240
                \0 → \0184 → ...time 3 → \0328
        2. use of INTAB[123]
            INTAB is index from 0 ~ 122, real access range is 0 ~ 122.
            The input s index is either [0-9] or [10#-26#].
                &the mapping relation is acutell muped to INTAB index
                    '0' - '9' → floor(INTAB.index(0 ~ 9))   ex: '0' -> INTAB[0], '0' + 1 -> INTAB[1]
                    '1#' - '9#' p→ floor(INTAB.index(0 ~ 9)) × 10 + INTAB.index(0 ~ 9); ex: '1#' -> floor(INTAB[10]) * 10 + INTAB[1]; // '10' difference with '1'
                    ∵ index from 0 need to plus one so that [1#] and '2' difference
        3. It use reverse to be faster?
            ∵ input digit sequence from [0 - 9], remember we can just to easy min prebuild
            char map and just use c at ascii table → acutually no big difference
            because we already reverse INTAB order
    Execution : 5ms
''',1

def getMoneySpent(keyboards, drives, b):
    max_spent = -1
    for keyboard in keyboards:
        for drive in drives:
            total_cost = keyboard + drive
            if total_cost <= b and total_cost > max_spent:
                max_spent = total_cost
    return max_spent

